  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In a frequency distribution histogram of the mathematics scores of 40 students in a class, the frequencies for the five groups \\([50,60)\\), \\([60,70)\\), \\([70,80)\\), \\([80,90)\\), and \\([90,100]\\) are 2, 6, 14, 12, and 6, respectively. How many students scored 60 points or above (including 60)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "38",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Scores of 60 points or above include the last four groups: \\(6+14+12+6=38\\) students.\n\nAlternative method 1: Subtract the excluded group\n\nOnly the group \\([50,60)\\) is below 60, and it contains 2 students. Every other student scored at least 60, since 60 belongs to \\([60,70)\\). Subtracting the excluded group from the class total gives \\(40-2=38\\) students.",
